<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh's Mongla port shut by workers' protest.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh's Mongla port shut by workers' protest.</headline>
<dateline>KHULNA, Bangladesh 1997-01-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>A workers' protest has shut Bangladesh's southern Mongla port, stranding 18 ships including one carrying wheat, port officials said on Sunday.</p>
<p>They said stevedores had refused to engage workers since Saturday night after about 300 men working in one section walked out demanding higher wages.</p>
<p>The port authority was holding talks with the Port Workers Association in a bid to bring the striking workers back to work.</p>
</text>
